{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/870083-lancea-et-sanctum","id":870083,"title":"Lancea et Sanctum","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-21T04:31:42-07:00","id":870083,"title":"Lancea et Sanctum","content":"I'm trying to understand the concept of the Lancea Sanctum. To me they seem to be the Sabbat of 1st ed but with a little catholic church thrown in. But most references make them sound rigid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4135-blue-thomas","name":"Blue Thomas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T04:57:01-07:00","id":870092,"title":"","content":"Ok, I'm going with VtR 2e Lancea, which has a tighter focus in my opinion.<br /> <br /> The Sanctified aren't monsters for monsters sake as most of the Sabbat is. They do not revel in their &quot;evilness&quot; because they are the next step in human evolution, or just because they're better than everyone else. As of 2e, this role belongs to the Circle: vampires are natural and their bestial natures are too, and so they must be embraced.<br /> The actions of the Kindred in the Lancea are that of a wolf-shepherd among sheep. They terrorize, corrupt and defile mortals to test them, and their supposed innocence. If you pass, you're good to go, they're probably even going to protect you (but I wouldn't count that as a blessing). If you fail, your life is ruined, or you're dead, or you become a good subject for the Embrace. Congratulations, you're a monster now! This is the official party line, of course. There are lots of heresies and sects out there.<br /> <br /> Their role as dark guides among humanity comes from God itself: that's their unholy mission for them. They've sinned and have been cursed, and so they must repent.<br /> And because Theban Sorcery is tied to Humanity, most practitioners must remain as human as possibile to retain their gifts. So, sort of paradoxically (but that's in theme!), Sanctified must act human to be the corrupters of humans. Which I think is kind of neat.<br /> <br /> Also, the Lancea is full of scholars and historians so you can play that angle a little bit. Vampire archaeologists! Not that <i>their</i> history is true: the Church likes to control history, so most documents are put somewhere safe (to be looked at by the most private eyes), or downright destroyed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Italian nuisance. English is my second language, so be patient!<br /> <br /> <b>My homebrew:</b><br /> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/270766-domain-light-from-a-dead-star-rome\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">[VtR 2e] Light From a Dead Star: Rome</span></a></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1117941-hunting-ground-the-past-is-another-country-rome\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><b>[WtF 2e] The Past Is Another Country: Rome</b></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3765-snesferatu","name":"SNESferatu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3765_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T05:45:01-07:00","id":870111,"title":"","content":"I'm not that familiar with the Sabbat, so I'm going to start at this with a blank slate. <br /> <br /> The Lancea et Sanctum are followers of the Word of Longinus, a vampire prophet who taught that vampires need to serve a purpose in this world. Yes, you are Damned, but that damnation has a meaning. The world is filled with sin, and the Kindred are called to cull sinners from the world, and to be the devil that tempts the righteous to ensure that they do have good intentions at heart. The LeS are the dark angels, who protect the herd of humanity from other predators, even as they feed on these people themselves. The angels of the Lord has gifted the Lance with Theban Sorcery, found in dark tomb of Egypt, in order to carry out their Mission. And different vampires have different takes on that mission. <br /> <br /> Due to the nature of Theban Sorcery (the reliance on Academics as a skill), this has actually turned the Lancea et Sanctum into a covenant that specializes in collecting vampire lore. Not just the occult, but the history and culture of vampires as a whole. The Lancea et Sanctum libraries are the most extensive of all Kindred covenants. A second aspect of Theban Sorcery is that it requires medial to high Humanity, which means that the Lance has developed methods of surviving (nay, thriving) as a vampire while maintaining one's Humanity.<br /> <br /> Yes, the Lance adopts the trappings of Catholicism (or Baptist, or Protestant, or any other Abrahamic religion). But it is only trappings. The Kindred don't really care if Jesus was the Son of God, or a prophet; that's a side note at best. What matters is that Longinus was Damned for living a life of sin and debauchery, and became the first vampire prophet to teach the Kindred God's plan for the undead. <br /> <br /> So far, I've been talking only about the vampires and their mission as it relates to mortals. Where it comes to other vampires? The Lance has the spiritual obligation to spread their faith and teachings to other vampires. And that involves a bit of underhanded action. The Lance not only collects historical and cultural texts and artificats, but they go out of their way to track down anything that deviates from the message they want to teach and hide it. Or destroy it. The Lance also has their paladins and Godslayers - Kindred that hunt down spirits or others that would rival or threaten the LeS spiritual mission. The Lancea et Sanctum serve as confessors to the Kindred city for those who've fallen too far, slipping their Humanity away, and helping to reclaim hir mind and soul from the Beast.<br /> <br /> Traditionally, the Lance is allied with the Invictus, due to their long and mutually beneficial history since the fall of Rome, and often share members, though that is not always a given.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T06:21:40-07:00","id":870130,"title":"","content":"I'll keep this short and sweet: the Lance exists as a coping mechanism. It's there to tell vampires that God has a purpose for them, and while it may be that of the devil and monster, that's still more comforting than &quot;enjoy a nihilistic eternity of hunger.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T06:58:11-07:00","id":870153,"title":"","content":"It's also the covenant with the most easily accepted reasoning for why you are a vampire, at least in the default western setting. Invictus and Carthian don't address it at all, the Circle will tell you something different for each cult, maybe it's natural maybe it's a gift of some dark goddess. The Ordo either says we don't know, not enough science, or God cursed you and we hate him. The latter is a common view, but the Ordo itself has modernized to emphasize the former view. The Sanctum says &quot;We know why you are a vampire, and more so, we know what to do next&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T18:47:30-07:00","id":870836,"title":"","content":"Sounds contradictory esp needing to keep high humanity. How do you do both? How can it be other religions when everything about it has a catholic veneer? I don't remember reading that in the Covenant book. So lets put up a scenerio. A human is walking down an alley and a vampire (not of the lance) attacks at the same time a member of the Lance comes upon the two. What happens? Is the Lance going to save the mortal? Or something more /less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4135-blue-thomas","name":"Blue Thomas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T19:06:06-07:00","id":870840,"title":"","content":"They have a high humanity through constantly interacting with humans, large focus on touchstones, etc. <br /> They are solidly Christian, but the trappings vary place to place. Snake-charming charismatic Appalachian Protestant-influenced Lance sects may focus on speaking in tongues and such like, while a powerful catholic-esque Bishop in Boston may summon a shadowy figure of a woman who makes each member of the congregation feel judged andunworthy. The covenant book goes over the various &quot;Rites&quot; that show how the covenant changes across places and cultures. Of course it also makes a cursory effort to fold Jewish and Muslim beliefs in, which fails to convince, but they seem to have dropped that in 2nd edition, which is good. <br /> <br /> Longinian faith is in keeping with the basic shared tenets of Christianity, where it barely matches those of Judaism and actively goes against those of Islam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T19:20:01-07:00","id":870853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blue Thomas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/870083-lancea-et-sanctum?p=870836#post870836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds contradictory esp needing to keep high humanity. How do you do both?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the tennents of Longinism aren't mutually exclusive with the requirements of maintaining high Humanity. And even when you lose Humanity, it can be regained.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blue Thomas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/870083-lancea-et-sanctum?p=870836#post870836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can it be other religions when everything about it has a catholic veneer? I don't remember reading that in the Covenant book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everything about it has an Abrahamic veneer, but Catholicism isn't the only Abrahamic religion. Belief in Longinus necessitates belief in Christ, but the Sanctum doesn't care if you believe he was the messiah, or a prophet, or just a holy man, or anything else. All that matters is that you believe he lived, and the man who pierced his side with the spear lived, and was Damned to vampirism. That's possible within a lot of religions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blue Thomas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/870083-lancea-et-sanctum?p=870836#post870836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So lets put up a scenerio. A human is walking down an alley and a vampire (not of the lance) attacks at the same time a member of the Lance comes upon the two. What happens? Is the Lance going to save the mortal? Or something more /less.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's not enough information in this scenario. Is the human a devout, God-fearing person? A righteous atheist? A wreched sinner? Does the Sanctified character know this? How does the Sanctified character interpret the Testament of Longinus? What is the Sanctified character's relationship with the other vampire? What is the Sanctified character's Humanity? There are a lot of variables that affect how any character would react to this kind of situation, beyond just Covenant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-21-2016, 10:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T19:35:15-07:00","id":870858,"title":"","content":"I can't help but imagine there would be a lecture.<br /> <br /> Provided the mortal wasn't under the Lancea vampire's protection, and the vampire wasn't strictly an enemy, perhaps the Lancea vampire would say something, not quite urging, to see if the vampire could control themselves while feeding. If not, they have something to hold over the vampire's head. If so, they can lecture them about how their humanity shines through by the grace of god and invite them to hear more at the services on Saturday night. They might usher the vampire off and dust off the human, helping them up and telling them what they did wrong, or right. There's a lot of ways to be a demon, after all. There's many different ways to play a vampire of the Lance, too, a lot of ways to view their Requiem, even within the confines of Lancea et Sanctum doctrine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-21T20:42:24-07:00","id":870890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/870083-lancea-et-sanctum?p=870840#post870840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Longinian faith is in keeping with the basic shared tenets of Christianity, where it barely matches those of Judaism and actively goes against those of Islam.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">How is it actively going against Islam? Islam recognizes that Jesus Christ was a prophet of Allah, just not the last prophet of Allah. Even most of modern Judaism recognizes that there was a man named </span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Yeshua and he was one of prophets of </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">YHVH Tzva'ot.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Not every Kindred Embraced </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">believing</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> in the </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Abrahamic</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> religions will view the Lancea Et Sanctum as the</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">i</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">r specific </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">concept of \u201cWe are cursed to be the Adversary/Satan to mortals\u201d as Gospel.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">But only but the most </span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Hasidic</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">of Jews and the most </span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">radical</span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> of Muslims will view Longinus\u2019s story as anything more than this \u201cA Roman soldier killed a prophet of YHVH/Allah/God and was cursed to be the Adversary of Man. He taught others of his plight and they carry on his curse to this day.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Catholic trappings can be dropped as long as it sums down to that statement: Soldier killed a prophet, God cursed him to be Adversary, Adversary passed on what he learned.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2704-deimosmasque","name":"DeimosMasque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T01:59:54-07:00","id":871061,"title":"","content":"I think it's less that the Lancea faith couldn't work with both Judaism and Islam, it's that you'd need to give it the proper text space to develop otherwise it looks a bit silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T03:59:54-07:00","id":871092,"title":"","content":"The LetS doctrine is independent of the mortal Abrahamic faiths, and practicing your mortal beliefs is shunned at best, persecuted at worst. It doesn't matter if you were a Catholic, a Muslim, a Jew or a pagan in life - as far as LetS is concerned, you are equally damned now, and the only gospel you should follow is that of Longinus. The aesthetics of the Church of the Damned are skewed towards Christianity because Christ is a central figure in their mythology and because the covenant evolved alongside Christianity in Rome and throughout the middle ages, but a devout Christian being Embraced and joining LetS will still have to learn a completely new doctrine that's barely compatible with his mortal beliefs. Equally, nothing's stopping a LetS member from viewing a wise Imam and a kind priest as equally righteous mortals and putting them both under Church's protection.<br /> <br /> Granted, mortal preconceptions and biases can and most likely will show through, but that's more a matter of particular Sanctified twisting the faith in support of their personal beliefs than something stemming from the doctrine itself. And twisting the doctrine to suit one's needs is something that happens across all faiths, from Christianity to Islam to paganism to militant atheism, so it's not like Lancea or its formerly Christian members will stand out in this regard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T05:39:59-07:00","id":871129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blue Thomas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/870083-lancea-et-sanctum?p=870836#post870836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds contradictory esp needing to keep high humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div> Confessors to help maintain/regain Humanity, take Banes, encourage Touchstones. The only contradiction is if you see them as acting entirely monstrous and inhuman, but that's not the point of the Lance. That's the purpose of the Circle of the Crone. The Lancea et Sanctum is actually closer to religious members of the Camarilla than they are to the religions of the Sabbat (which are found in the CotC). The Lance doesn't teach its members to revel in monstrocity, they teach them to channel it with a clear minded purpose. Even a Lance that kills criminals will simply take a bane and no longer lose Humanity for killing sinners in the name of God.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How do you do both? How can it be other religions when everything about it has a catholic veneer? </div> </div> </div> The Catholic touch is the most common version of the LeS in the US and Western Europe, but its not absolute. Different denominations (called Creeds) is exist. Different cities have different trappings. You are expected to do that with every covenant, in fact - change the trappings depending on the needs of your city and story. The Circle of the Crone has vampire-wicca trappings in many areas, but turns to voodoun more commonly in New Orleans, or adopts Hindu trappings in areas influenced by that religion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't remember reading that in the Covenant book. So lets put up a scenerio. A human is walking down an alley and a vampire (not of the lance) attacks at the same time a member of the Lance comes upon the two. What happens? Is the Lance going to save the mortal? Or something more /less. </div> </div> </div> Depends entirely on the situation and the Kindred involved. Is that mortal someone under the Lance's protection? Has the vampire fallen into frenzy? Why is the Lance and other vampire in the same territory? Who does the territory belong to? Is the Lance a hardline zealot, or does she have a more personal-everyone-must-choose stance? There are plenty of other questions we could ask as well that would change the answer.<br /> <br /> Context is king, and such scenarios have too many questions to answer. It all depends on the situation and individuals involved. There are some situations where a Lance would get involved, and others where she would not.<br /> <br /> <br /> Given what you've said previously, however, I think that you feel that the Lance should universally approve of violently draining humans, as per Sabbat. There are plenty of reasons here why the Lance, as a whole, would not approve of such baseless behavior. Vampires have a purpose, and senselessly feeding on a random person does not serve that purpose. Now the Circle of the Crone would have lots of people that would approve of such predatorial behavior. In fact, its pretty much what happens in the 2e's little fiction blurb at the top of the Covenant description.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 04-22-2016, 08:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T07:37:47-07:00","id":871206,"title":"","content":"It goes against Muslim beliefs because it says that there was an earlier set of revelation not overwritten by the Quran. Muhammad is not only the last prophet but the SEAL of the prophets. His revelation is final, previous revelation is no longer valid. So to believe that the revelations of Longinus are still valid today you would have to deny a basic tenet of your mortal faith in a way that a Christian wouldn't. It would be equivalent to if being a Longinian required a Christian to deny that Jesus was the son of God, as all teachings were predicated on that. <br /> <br /> Any religious Muslim covenant has to have its basis in purported revelations from Muhammad. You can't have revelations before being still valid, or any revelations after (with the exception of the Mahdi/Messiah in some faiths). <br /> <br /> Now the LeS may see all vampires as being under their purview, but that's no different than if all Jews saw all other Abraham's religions as being little more than Jews led astray. It's condescending, and not at all accurate, and doesn't mean that Christians and Muslims can easily become Jews without sacrificing their previous beliefs. <br /> <br /> Luckily, one can make a believable Muslim covenant in the LeS model; Muhammad only dictated the Quran and it wasn't written down until later, as people memorized specific parts or wrote them down on animal shoulder blades. When the Caliph collected the pets and organized them together, it is alleged that some parts were missed: several people had to corroborate that the verse was legitimate for it to be included. What if, later, a strange cryptic verse, written in blood on a human shoulder bone, was discovered, seeming to allude to the vampiric condition? That could be the starting point of a new covenant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T08:00:57-07:00","id":871233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/870083-lancea-et-sanctum?p=871206#post871206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So to believe that the revelations of Longinus are still valid today you would have to deny a basic tenet of your mortal faith in a way that a Christian wouldn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I must have read some other Bible, because the revelation that blood-sucking undead monsters not only exist, but were created by God for the specific purpose of tormenting the living undermines every tenet of Christianity that I'm aware of.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Whether you're a Jew, a Christian, or a Muslim, the creed of Lancea Sanctum is going to be a big shock for you. It acknowledges the same God (inasmuch as these three religions agree upon the nature of God), but it also preaches that the faiths you know are meant for the living and living only, while the undead have their own covenant with God. Whether you put your faith in the Torah, New Testament or Quran matters not now that you are dead and cursed. It's a completely different religion, stemming from the same root belief but no more compatible with any other than Judaism is compatible with Islam. Muslims are in the same boat as everyone else as far as Sanctified are concerned, and there is only one gospel for the dead, take it or leave it. That is if they allow you to leave it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":582,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","user":"Morangias","date":". 04-22-2016, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T08:38:17-07:00","id":871276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/870083-lancea-et-sanctum?p=871206#post871206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It goes against Muslim beliefs because it says that there was an earlier set of revelation not overwritten by the Quran. Muhammad is not only the last prophet but the SEAL of the prophets. His revelation is final, previous revelation is no longer valid. So to believe that the revelations of Longinus are still valid today you would have to deny a basic tenet of your mortal faith in a way that a Christian wouldn't. It would be equivalent to if being a Longinian required a Christian to deny that Jesus was the son of God, as all teachings were predicated on that.</div> </div> </div> </div> For humans. The basic belief of the Lance is that you are no longer human, and human teachings don't apply. Going Lance after being Christian means that you have to accept that the Blood of the Lamb didn't redeem your sins by dying on the Cross. And that's as central to Christianity as Muhammad being the last prophet is to Islam. No mortal religion is a match to Longinian teachings, and trying to say that one religion has to deny basic tenants while others do not is flat out wrong. Muslim, Christian, Jew, other, you name it. At best, the Lance has superficial similarties to the Abrahamic religions. The actual dogma is flat out different from any mortal religion. <br /> <br /> The Lance isn't Catholic. Its not Christian, its not Muslim, its not Jewish. We're talking about a vampire specific religion that calls for a Humanity check when you join. The whole point is that you are coming to understand you are no longer human, and different rules apply to you. Islam is not special in this regard. Hells, the Abrahamic religions and the Lance aren't special in this regard. The CotC, if anything, is even shockingly more different than their mortal counterpart religions of Wicca, Voodoun, and others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now the LeS may see all vampires as being under their purview, but that's no different than if all Jews saw all other Abraham's religions as being little more than Jews led astray. It's condescending, and not at all accurate, and doesn't mean that Christians and Muslims can easily become Jews without sacrificing their previous beliefs. </div> </div> </div> True, but that's pretty much how most religions work when they spread. Pretty much every dominant religion we've had throughout history has acted that way at one point or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T08:50:54-07:00","id":871297,"title":"","content":"Also, <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/870083-lancea-et-sanctum?p=871206#post871206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Luckily, one can make a believable Muslim covenant in the LeS model; Muhammad only dictated the Quran and it wasn't written down until later, as people memorized specific parts or wrote them down on animal shoulder blades. When the Caliph collected the pets and organized them together, it is alleged that some parts were missed: several people had to corroborate that the verse was legitimate for it to be included. What if, later, a strange cryptic verse, written in blood on a human shoulder bone, was discovered, seeming to allude to the vampiric condition? That could be the starting point of a new covenant.</div> </div> </div> </div> This has already been covered by history in the Ancient Mysteries book. The Banu Shaitan started off as Qaran scholars that apparently had revelations beyond the human verses that told them the purpose of vampires to test and protect the faithful, much as the Lance does, and had equal command of Theban Sorcery. The Benu Shaitan remained as a separate covenant until the 19th century, until an agreement between the two led to them considering each other as branches of the same covenant and God.<br /> <br /> So, in the end, there's very little difference between the Lance and the Benu Shaitan, just a difference in what trappings. While there might also be a few differences with the details, the central tenants of the two remain pretty much identical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T11:14:58-07:00","id":871501,"title":"","content":"Eh, I still disagree. Having studied all three Abrahamic religions in detail, the Lance still strikes me as uniquely Christian, in history, in world-view, in teachings. I can imagine being a Christian and being told &quot;When Christ died, the soldier who killed him was cursed, and we follow the teachings of the soldier who killed him because he got revelations from God.&quot; The answer to that is &quot;Ok, sure.&quot; And then the Christian becomes a Longinian. If I'm Jewish, it might involve a &quot;Ok, not sure why Christ is so special, but ok.&quot; And then the Jew becomes a Longinian. If I'm Muslim, it goes &quot;Ok, sure, but why is his revelation still valid?&quot; To accept that it is valid, I have to accept that Muhammad is no longer the seal of the prophets, have to recant the Shahadda, and thus have to STOP being a Muslim before I become a Longinian. This specific point here is where things go wonky. The dogma FOLLOWING this point may be uniquely Longinian, but the basic premise of it, the premise that the revelations of someone who is not Muhammad are still valid, excludes Muslims.<br /> <br /> Do you see where I'm going with this? The Longinian faith is solidly an Abrahamic faith (belief in the Abrahamic God), one whose origin story (and subsequent development) is inextricably tied with Christianity. It may be a unique Abrahamic faith that is meant solely for the undead, but that doesn't erase it's ties and pre-requisite beliefs.<br /> The Banu Shaitan have a similar issue. They have to claim that a revelation AFTER Muhammad is valid (outside of the Mahdi, a special case), and thus renounce that Muhammad is the last prophet, and that's a sticking point.<br /> <br /> Now, specific points of dogma may contradict with Christianity or Judaism, such as the wiping of sin that you pointed out above. But that's a specific point of dogma, one that is, to my knowledge, debated in Christianity anyhow. The basic premise that the dogma is built upon, that there is a reason to follow Longinus at all, does not contradict Christianity or Judaism. You can be a Longinian, and still believe that Christ was the Son of God, and that his coming was to replace the Old Testament with the New, or you can be a Longinian and believe that Christ was merely a new prophet, but you cannot be a Longinian and still believe that Muhammad's revelation is the final word of God.<br /> <br /> Edit: plus looking over my previous posts on the subject, I forgot the point that you would have to deny that the Qur'an is the literal word of God, as the Qur'an literally states that Jesus never died but was uplifted from the cross alive into heaven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","user":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","date":". 04-22-2016, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T11:47:05-07:00","id":871551,"title":"","content":"It just depends on if you're willing to accept that Muhammad's revelation was only the final word of God <i>as it pertains to humans</i>, and that God gave different words to different prophets pertaining to vampires. That's a pill some (formerly) Muslim vampires will be able to swallow, and some won't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T11:54:31-07:00","id":871563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/870083-lancea-et-sanctum?p=871501#post871501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you see where I'm going with this? The Longinian faith is solidly an Abrahamic faith (belief in the Abrahamic God), one whose origin story (and subsequent development) is inextricably tied with Christianity. It may be a unique Abrahamic faith that is meant solely for the undead, but that doesn't erase it's ties and pre-requisite beliefs.<br /> The Banu Shaitan have a similar issue. They have to claim that a revelation AFTER Muhammad is valid (outside of the Mahdi, a special case), and thus renounce that Muhammad is the last prophet, and that's a sticking point.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Iblic Creed, the Islamic variant of the Lancea et Sanctum, believe that while Jesus was a holy prophet, he was before Mohammed.<br /> <br /> About their specific Creed it says this, ''Individual Ibn-Shaitan must follow an inverted interpretation of the Five Pillars of Islam, which claims that Allah chose all vampires to challenge the faith of mortal man.'<br /> <br /> But that's first edition. Second edition seems to have opened up the concepts involved further, and I can see a more specifically dedicated Islamic covenant that is unrelated to the Lancea et Sanctum existing. Possibly several.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-22-2016, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T12:21:43-07:00","id":871593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/870083-lancea-et-sanctum?p=871501#post871501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you see where I'm going with this?</div> </div> </div> </div> I do, I just disagree. For one, Muhammad was a human prophet who delivered words to humans, not djinn. For another, Dark Miracles are given through revelation and prophesy to vampires, and that is an ongoing thing that continues to the modern day. There are several kinds of angels that continue to appear in the CofD to make modern prophets - that's one of the basis of the CofD.<br /> <br /> Some people will have trouble giving up their mortal faith for a vampire one. And that's fine, every vampire, no matter their mortal religion, goes through that same question. But its not an insurmountable hurdle, or something unique to Islam. I also think that, for all that you claim that Islam needs to be treated differently, you are remarkably blase about Judaism and just shoving them into a Christian-lite category, which is offensive to that faith. You are just assuming that the Jewish will be just as ready to accept Longinus as any Christian, and that's debatable. <br /> <br /> Let me ask you a question - are you a Muslim?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T17:03:03-07:00","id":871891,"title":"","content":"I got the sense from reading the 2e write-up of the Lance that they'd made them more clearly Christian-like while also saying they're not really like Christians, and that it's more of a superficial relationship between their beliefs.<br /> <br /> Honestly, the beef I have with the concept of the Banu Shaitan or the Dammitic Creed is that I don't really feel there's a need to make the Chapel &amp; Spear the final word on Abrahamic Covenants. If I were to include them in a game, I'd probably try to make them slightly more divergent from Longinian faith, or try to conceptualize them as different covenants entirely, or in some cases maybe as ideologies shared between Kindred rather than a covenant in a strict sense.<br /> <br /> I only bring this up because I think elements of those ideas were emergent from the idea that everything had to be crammed into the Big Five in 1e, which 2e has pretty clearly moved away from. There's plenty of fertile ground for exploring how a sect of vampires who base their beliefs in Judaism or Islam might be like, as well as their relationship with the <i>Testament of Longinus</i>.<br /> <br /> All this talk is entirely separate from the concept of whether a Christian or Muslim or Jewish person turnt Vampire actually reject their faith in the first place. Some might just stick to it, theoretical contradictions and all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T17:12:45-07:00","id":871894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/870083-lancea-et-sanctum?p=871891#post871891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All this talk is entirely separate from the concept of whether a Christian or Muslim or Jewish person turnt Vampire actually reject their faith in the first place. Some might just stick to it, theoretical contradictions and all.</div> </div> </div> </div> The Septimi are based around it, in fact!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-22T19:27:17-07:00","id":871988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/870083-lancea-et-sanctum?p=871891#post871891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got the sense from reading the 2e write-up of the Lance that they'd made them more clearly Christian-like while also saying they're not really like Christians, and that it's more of a superficial relationship between their beliefs.<br /> <br /> Honestly, the beef I have with the concept of the Banu Shaitan or the Dammitic Creed is that I don't really feel there's a need to make the Chapel &amp; Spear the final word on Abrahamic Covenants. If I were to include them in a game, I'd probably try to make them slightly more divergent from Longinian faith, or try to conceptualize them as different covenants entirely, or in some cases maybe as ideologies shared between Kindred rather than a covenant in a strict sense.<br /> <br /> I only bring this up because I think elements of those ideas were emergent from the idea that everything had to be crammed into the Big Five in 1e, which 2e has pretty clearly moved away from. There's plenty of fertile ground for exploring how a sect of vampires who base their beliefs in Judaism or Islam might be like, as well as their relationship with the <i>Testament of Longinus</i>.<br /> <br /> All this talk is entirely separate from the concept of whether a Christian or Muslim or Jewish person turnt Vampire actually reject their faith in the first place. Some might just stick to it, theoretical contradictions and all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with all of this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T03:29:48-07:00","id":872262,"title":"","content":"Even if you call it a different covenant with a different history, they're likely going to have the same overall archetype as the Lance, as well as the same overall teachings. And, honeslty, the vast majority of players I'm familiar with don't really care that much about a grand history that you write up for a group. At best, its a footnote. They care about the night-to-night operation, how it informs their characters, and the personalities involved. Of course, they also care about the benefits.<br /> <br /> So, from a practical, game design standpoint, what exactly is different here beyond the history and the religious overtones? Because that's something that should be different for every city you devise, and for every covenant. Are the factions notably different? Any benefits that should be different? The reasons to join? How they act when in power or out of power? What the goals are? How the priests and laiety act?<br /> <br /> At least, when Ancient Mysteries / Bloodlines covered vampire-voodoun, the highlighted stark differences from the Circle beyond the superficial. We have different practices, different belief systems, different benefits, different relationships, different reasons to join, different drives, different goals.<br /> <br /> Its easy to say &quot;Oh, they should be their own covenant!&quot; Its harder to put in practice. So, Ancient Mysteries covered a look at the Muslim version with their own book (modified Qaran) and didn't worship Longinus. They have a unique history. What exactly should be different about the Benu Shaitan to make them even further different than what's mentioned? Because history and trappings seem to be already there. What else?<br /> <br /> As far as I'm concerned, this is where the conversation fails. People want a different covenant for Islam, but never explains a difference beyond a reflavored Qaran as the basis instead of the Testament of Longinus, and a different history. We have both with the Benu Shaitan, but that's apparently not enough. So, lets start. In fact, I would absolutely love to hear from an actual Muslim or Jew on their take of a vampire version of their faiths. But, while I've had Hindu gaming friends, I've never actually met a Muslim or Jewish gamer to talk with. I've never seen any on this board who want to speak up about the matter, possibly because they're afraid of backlash. All I've ever seen are armchair theorists who cliam some background in study, but never anyone who actually practices. <br /> <br /> So, when all is said and done, I want to hear it. What exactly would be different here in a way that stands out in a game?<br /> <br /> Also, I feel that there's a theme of anti-semitism here, giving that people are happy to shove the Jewish into the Longinian church, while we have to treat Islam special. Simply treating the Jewish as pre-Christians is insulting to their cultur and beliefs. You either have to consider all three Abrahamics as separate, or none. Anything else is just marginalizing and insulting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 04-23-2016, 06:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T04:13:39-07:00","id":872267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/870083-lancea-et-sanctum?p=871297#post871297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in the end, there's very little difference between the Lance and the Benu Shaitan, just a difference in what trappings. While there might also be a few differences with the details, the central tenants of the two remain pretty much identical.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nevermind that it is first edition, I feel like it's worth pointing out that the design space the Banu Shaitan inhabited was an origin story for the Iblic Creed, so if there's any reason to be leery of using them as-is it's just that you could probably do more with the concept without the implicit limitation of &quot;these guys have to eventually become Sanctified.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T04:15:12-07:00","id":872269,"title":"","content":"Here, I'll even start. Lets homebrew this. Covenant writeups have the following format:<br /> <br /> Title, and a subtitle with an alternative name. <br /> Fiction blurb<br /> You want to join the covenant because:<br /> The Big Picture:<br /> Where we came from:<br /> Our Practices<br /> Nicknames<br /> Stereotypes<br /> When we are in power<br /> When we are in trouble:<br /> <br /> And then, there's covenant advantages / merits that need to be considered. I personally think the Lancea et Sanctum merits and magic are already a match, given the focus on libaries and scholarship both have (I've even been vocal about having official muslim- and jewish- themed theban rituals published in some book), but if you want the covenant to be different, then there should be something different here. <br /> <br /> I'll start a new thread, and people can write down what they want to see in the different sections.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T04:17:25-07:00","id":872270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/870083-lancea-et-sanctum?p=872267#post872267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nevermind that it is first edition, I feel like it's worth pointing out that the design space the Banu Shaitan inhabited was an origin story for the Iblic Creed, so if there's any reason to be leery of using them as-is it's just that you could probably do more with the concept without the implicit limitation of &quot;these guys have to eventually become Sanctified.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> Then forget the Iblic Creed part. Its 2e, like you said, so we can rewrite 1e history so that doesn't happen. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T04:23:05-07:00","id":872272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/870083-lancea-et-sanctum?p=872270#post872270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Then forget the Iblic Creed part. Its 2e, like you said, so we can rewrite 1e history so that doesn't happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I meant was that their concept prior to actually becoming the Iblic Creed is heavily influenced by the purpose of having them eventually join the Sanctified, but that's a cool way to approach it. <i>Ancient Mysteries </i>provides a somewhat interesting framework to work with.<br /> <br /> I think there was a thread about this awhile back where some really neat ideas got bandied about, so I'll try to dig that up for a new one discussing this concept further.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T04:23:31-07:00","id":872273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/870083-lancea-et-sanctum?p=871593#post871593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I do, I just disagree. For one, Muhammad was a human prophet who delivered words to humans, not djinn. For another, Dark Miracles are given through revelation and prophesy to vampires, and that is an ongoing thing that continues to the modern day. There are several kinds of angels that continue to appear in the CofD to make modern prophets - that's one of the basis of the CofD.<br /> <br /> Some people will have trouble giving up their mortal faith for a vampire one. And that's fine, every vampire, no matter their mortal religion, goes through that same question. But its not an insurmountable hurdle, or something unique to Islam. I also think that, for all that you claim that Islam needs to be treated differently, you are remarkably blase about Judaism and just shoving them into a Christian-lite category, which is offensive to that faith. You are just assuming that the Jewish will be just as ready to accept Longinus as any Christian, and that's debatable.<br /> <br /> Let me ask you a question - are you a Muslim?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I'm raised Jewish, I'm more knowledgeable about Islam though. That's why I hedge my bets on Judaism and the LeS; I don't outright see anything that forbids Judaism from following latter prophecies, but I do know that they'll have serious questions about why Jesus was so special, when many Prophets were persecuted and killed. I did post the basis of a Covenant a while ago, but I can't seem to find it now. It wasn't in the new format anyhow. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T05:49:00-07:00","id":872304,"title":"","content":"Humm after reading all this, I'm incline to think of it this way: <br /> 1. It's a christian covenant only that believe in Christ but eschewed view of him, since they think he's cursed them. I might even put in the whole Cain thing and smash it up with the covenant making it more Anne Rice.<br /> 2. I like the idea of other religions having Covenants. I can see the Assamites from 1st ed reworked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4135-blue-thomas","name":"Blue Thomas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T07:08:17-07:00","id":872332,"title":"","content":"IMO the conception of Longinus as the key figure is more interesting than Caine, but its up to you what you do in your own game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T07:10:43-07:00","id":872334,"title":"","content":"I always figured the Cain figure could be a more Judaeocentric origin myth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T07:12:25-07:00","id":872336,"title":"","content":"I'm interested how Cain could work with clearly Longinian faith. ( I'm only passer by on <b>Requiem</b> ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-23-2016, 03:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T10:38:01-07:00","id":872488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/870083-lancea-et-sanctum?p=872336#post872336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I;m interested how Cain could work with clearly Longinian faith. ( I'm only passer by on <b>Requiem</b> ).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well Cain is only how vampires got there. Longinis didn't create vampires. Right? I'm not certain about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4135-blue-thomas","name":"Blue Thomas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T12:00:18-07:00","id":872569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/870083-lancea-et-sanctum?p=872336#post872336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I;m interested how Cain could work with clearly Longinian faith. ( I'm only passer by on <b>Requiem</b> ).</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember, straight from 2005, that in the Nomads sourcebook there was a NPC who followed a heresy of the Lancea that believed that Longinus wasn't cursed by the blood of Jesus, but Embraced at the crucifixion by another <i>ancient</i> vampire that was himself directly cursed from God. This original vampire is never named, but he's Cain. It was a not-so-subtle nod to VtM.<br /> <br /> So, if you want, you can put Cain there. It goes against established canon, as probably there isn't a singular origin for vampirekind, but no one is going to stop you.<br /> And yes, Longinus <i>did not </i>create vampires, he's not even that old compared to some other parasites out there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Italian nuisance. English is my second language, so be patient!<br /> <br /> <b>My homebrew:</b><br /> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/270766-domain-light-from-a-dead-star-rome\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">[VtR 2e] Light From a Dead Star: Rome</span></a></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1117941-hunting-ground-the-past-is-another-country-rome\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><b>[WtF 2e] The Past Is Another Country: Rome</b></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3765-snesferatu","name":"SNESferatu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3765_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T12:33:16-07:00","id":872596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blue Thomas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/870083-lancea-et-sanctum?p=872488#post872488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well Cain is only how vampires got there. Longinis didn't create vampires. Right? I'm not certain about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lancea et Sanctum would say that Longinus was not the first vampire, but he was the first vampire to accept his role in God's plan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T20:18:06-07:00","id":872836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/870083-lancea-et-sanctum?p=872596#post872596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lancea et Sanctum would say that Longinus was not the first vampire, but he was the first vampire to accept his role in God's plan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4135-blue-thomas","name":"Blue Thomas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T20:49:32-07:00","id":872854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blue Thomas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/870083-lancea-et-sanctum?p=872836#post872836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! It is that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Testament of Longinus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And there appeared to me a blinding light, and I cowered in the tomb, thinking the sun had risen, but there stood before me archangel Vahishtael, with black wings and the heads of a calf, a serpent and a wolf, and holding a spear like the Spear I still held, and he spoke to me, and said: <br /> \u201cfear me, Longinus. for I am the messenger of your purpose.<br /> \u201cThe Damned are many, and they are denied salvation. <br /> \u201cBut the Damned serve as the sign to humanity of the price of sin, and to make mortals fear and to understand that their lives are brief and full of pain, and they can only see the most pitiful reflection of the glories of heaven, for they do not see clearly, but see as if through a blurred mirror, and the Damned do not see through the mirror at all.<br /> \u201cAnd it is the lot of the Damned to take the blood of mortals, that mortals might know that they will die, and that their only salvation is in the next life.<br /> \u201cAnd it is your lot to go and give this message to all of the Damned, that they might know God\u2019s purpose for them and rejoice. <br /> \u201cNow go, Longinus, and spread the Word to all the Damned.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not a fan of the covenant myself, but I do find it interesting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T05:30:34-07:00","id":873026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/870083-lancea-et-sanctum?p=872336#post872336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm interested how Cain could work with clearly Longinian faith. ( I'm only passer by on <b>Requiem</b> ).</div> </div> </div> </div>In Requiem for Rome there was a Sanctified heressy that believed in Cain as the first vampire.<br /> <br /> By the way, RfR also stablishes that the Lancea et Sanctum was originally a jewish vsmpiric cult (the Sanctum) in the Collegia Peregrine.<br /> Around first century, the opened to small Gnostic, Christian and marginsl vampiric faith from the Empire. The Longinians (the Lancea) was one of those faiths, but it grew until finally they became the main faction of the cult and broke with the Collegia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T01:48:13-07:00","id":1140449,"title":"","content":"NOTE: I wrote this for another similar thread, I figured it would make sense to post it here, too. If you see some references to what others have said, it might be from the other thread.<br /> <br /> Hi, everybody,<br /> <br /> I am Muslim and I bumped into this thread as I was planning to narrate a chronicle set in Cordoba in the year 1000 CE, so culturally-Muslim vampires will feature heavily.<br /> <br /> Note: I only became aware of the Banu Shaytan and Iblic Creed stuff reading your posts, and I am going to check them out immediately. Thank you.<br /> <br /> First, to be clear: Islam's abrogations of previous revelations does not mean they stop being true and of divine origin. It simply means that the norms they set are no more binding and that, if they say something explicitly denied by the Quran (such as Jesus - peace be upon him - being the Son of God), that is to be considered a human addition. Beyond this, Muslims throughout history, even pious ones reputed to be saints/walis, have had all sorts of attitudes to previous religions. Also, there are some Muslims who do not believe in abrogation and see previous religions as still valid, though they are few and criticized for this. They exist, nonetheless, so Muslim-cultured Kindred might well claim similar ideas.<br /> <br /> My personal take on the Lancea et Sanctum as seen by vampires in Muslim lands is this: when Islam appeared, the Byzantine Empire was mostly Sanctified (i.e.: LeS), Arabia was Circle of the Crone and Persia (Zoroastrianism) was CotC or something else (still need to figure it out, since Persian stuff does not feature in my Cordoba chronicle).<br /> Early human converts to Islam, once embraced, would not find Muslim guides in their vampirism. The closest thing they would find were Sanctified teachers. Longinism would make more sense to them than adapting Islam to vampirism because:<br /> 1) Islam's religious precepts are evidently not appliable to vampires;<br /> 2) only God can issue religious norms, so vampires can't just take the five pillars, dietary restrictions and other rules and adapt them to vampires (like five prayers at night, don't drink blood of drunkards or pig-eaters, starve to torpor/frenzy in Ramadan, etc), as one would need divine authority for that. Regarding the prayers, I prefer not making them perform any of the five daily prayers, not even the night ones, on the basis that, drinking human blood and being more or less walking corpses, they would be considered ritually impure in various schools of Islamic law, thus being forbidden from performing the five obligatory prayers (although they can perform other forms of prayer that do not require ritual purity, such as dhikr - the remembrance of God - or dua - supplication and personal conversation with God);<br /> 3) Muslims acknowledge previous prophets, including Jesus (peace be upon him), so the tale of Longinus receiving guidance can work. Theologically, he may be classed as a wali (saint) from the community of Jesus, as opposed to a prophet in the strict Islamic theological sense, and this would make things easier;<br /> 4) surah al-Jinn (72nd surah of the Quran) says some Jinn were listening to the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) once while he was reciting the Quran and recognised its divine origin. In general, Jinn are believed to be of different kinds, to descend from Iblis/Lucifer/the Devil/Shaytan/Satan, to be responsible for part of polytheism (as jinns made humans worship them as gods), to be able to mate with humans and have offspring from them at times, to have free will, to follow different religions - the same humans follow, since, as far as I learnt, they do not get their own prophets but are guided by human prophets and saints, hence the idea of Longinus being a wali/saint instead of a vampire prophet. Muslim-cultured vampires may see themselves as a sub-species of Jinn (the Strix may well be another sub-species), especially if this is how Arabian pre-Islamic vampires saw themselves. Whichever vampire claimed to have interacted with the Prophet (peace be upon him) or his Companions and received instructions from them may have simply said that the main order was to carry on with Longinism, just knowing that Jesus is not God or His Son, etc., but without prescribed rules that differ from Longinism;<br /> 5) the Quran and the Hadith do not mention (to my knowledge) what rules Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) set for the Jinn, although it's generally understood that they did receive rules from him and previous prophets (peace be upon them all), so whatever rules Longinism imposes on vampires, that can be claimed as the rules set for them;<br /> 6) Longinism does not see Longinus as God, but only as a kind of prophet. This does not overtly contrast the Islamic creed, although it would make it slightly in theological debates easier to see Longinus as a wali/saint or sort of mystical disciple of Jesus. As a wali, he could still receive visions and inspirations, though there are some slight theological differences between walis and prophets.<br /> 7) there are various interpretations of the verses of the Quran about the crucifixion. It's enough to say that Longinian &quot;Muslim&quot; vampires stick to the view that Jesus (peace be upon him) was put on the cross, pierced by Longinus, and then taken up to heaven (before dying). <br /> <br /> In my setting, a Lancea et Sanctum Council was called in Damascus in 800 CE and established that the Church of Longinus was independent of the developments of human religions and its members were free to believe that Muhammad (peace be upon him) was a prophet or not, settling the issue for most adherents (obviously there can always be minor conflicts and divisions here and there, but they don't entail the forming of a wholly different Covenant). Moreover, vampires were not meant to push humans to one or the other Abrahamic religion, as this could effectively harm the appeal of that religion, but only remind humans of God, making them fear Him, tempt them to test them, and fight the Circle of the Crone and any vampire who promoted polytheism or atheism.<br /> <br /> I assume that there are vampires who carry on their mortal religion (whether Islam or Christianity or Judaism or other), but these usually act alone and have not formed proper Covenants that can rival with the LeS. It is quite common for new vampires, too, to hang onto one's mortal religion for a while, but this is usually temporary. One exception that I plan to include in the Chronicle is a group of vampire vampire-hunters called &quot;at-Tawwabun&quot; (the Repentant), who believe the only way to be forgiven by God is by killing other vampires and feeding only from animals forbidden to Muslims (ex.: pigs and predatory animals). This would be an antagonist covenant, however, not open to players. I have more interesting ideas about them, but I'll share them in time, God willing.<br /> <br /> In my Cordoba, the Bishop/Great Imam of the Lancea et Sanctum/ar-Rumh wal-Quds (I use double names to reflect the double culture of the vampires of Muslim Spain) has imposed on the city's vampire to feed only from sinful humans and not to kill the kine, unless they were condemned to death by the human authorities. In addition to this, Longinians are encouraged to shepherd the flock they belonged to in life (vampires who were Muslim prey on Muslims and vampires who were Christian prey on Christians), as they are most likely to understand how to remind their victims of God, but this is only an encouragement.<br /> <br /> I hope all the above makes sense. I am going to read the material about the Banu Shaytan and see how that is, God willing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T02:17:54-07:00","id":1144674,"title":"","content":"A very serious Question regarding this Covenant.<br /> <br /> In the Second Edition is the &quot;Book of Longinus &quot; as it is printed in the first edition canon? There is a reference to the book of Longinus on page 42 but is it referenced as a generic text that the St can make whatever he wants or its the printed Book?<br /> <br /> I ask this that in the Second Editions and the printed material that followed the Covenants are purposely left vague except the basic tenets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Member of the Requiem For Greece Storyteller Team<br /> <br /> City of Athens Storyteller<br /> <br /> Exalted funboy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/823-balancer","name":"Balancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T04:59:14-07:00","id":1146024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Balancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/870083-lancea-et-sanctum?p=1144674#post1144674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A very serious Question regarding this Covenant.<br /> <br /> In the Second Edition is the &quot;Book of Longinus &quot; as it is printed in the first edition canon? There is a reference to the book of Longinus on page 42 but is it referenced as a generic text that the St can make whatever he wants or its the printed Book?<br /> <br /> I ask this that in the Second Editions and the printed material that followed the Covenants are purposely left vague except the basic tenets.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to think in terms of the first edition, given that the second one is still developing (in terms of more elaborated background and details for clans, covenants and bloodlines. That being said, it's up to the storyteller whether to use the published Testament of Longinus or something else of his own device but with the same name. I read parts of the published Testament of Longinus after inventing this version of the Covenant and realised that some passages of the Testament of Longinus would be problematic (supporting clearly Catholic doctrines in contrast with Islam), but one way I dealt with it is that &quot;Muslim&quot; LeS tend to see those as the point of view of either Longinus or the Monachus, conditioned by the ideas of the time, but not actually part of the revelation. Generally speaking, they regard the Testament of Longinus as revealed in its general message, but not in its specific wording, and Longinus, not being fully a prophet, was not immune from error. Also, the Testament of Longinus, like the Torah and the Gospel, is considered corruptible, unlike the text of the Quran. So, basically, anything in the Testament of Longinus that doesn't fit with &quot;Islam&quot; (as a LeS &quot;Muslim&quot; vampire would take it) is considered a human addition or error, even though the text in itself keeps being followed and revered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T07:05:59-07:00","id":1146047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/870083-lancea-et-sanctum?p=872273#post872273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but I do know that they'll have serious questions about why Jesus was so special, when many Prophets were persecuted and killed. I did post the basis of a Covenant a while ago, but I can't seem to find it now. It wasn't in the new format anyhow.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasnt that much that Jesus was so special but that the hitting on jesus with a spear was the culmination of Longinus perfect shit-head day. His entire life was a constant stream of sin, even hitting jesus with the spear was done out of laziness or drunkenness (dont remember which). <br /> <br /> To the point God (of whatever creed you choose) said. &quot;Okay, dude eternal curse for you. You cant be so much of a shit head without me casting something on your head&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T08:32:38-07:00","id":1146066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/870083-lancea-et-sanctum?p=1140449#post1140449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Early human converts to Islam, once embraced, would not find Muslim guides in their vampirism. The closest thing they would find were Sanctified teachers. Longinism would make more sense to them than adapting Islam to vampirism because:<br /> 1) Islam's religious precepts are evidently not appliable to vampires;<br /> 2) only God can issue religious norms, so vampires can't just take the five pillars, dietary restrictions and other rules and adapt them to vampires (like five prayers at night, don't drink blood of drunkards or pig-eaters, starve to torpor/frenzy in Ramadan, etc), as one would need divine authority for that. Regarding the prayers, I prefer not making them perform any of the five daily prayers, not even the night ones, on the basis that, drinking human blood and being more or less walking corpses, they would be considered ritually impure in various schools of Islamic law, thus being forbidden from performing the five obligatory prayers (although they can perform other forms of prayer that do not require ritual purity, such as dhikr - the remembrance of God - or dua - supplication and personal conversation with God);<br /> 3) Muslims acknowledge previous prophets, including Jesus (peace be upon him), so the tale of Longinus receiving guidance can work. Theologically, he may be classed as a wali (saint) from the community of Jesus, as opposed to a prophet in the strict Islamic theological sense, and this would make things easier;</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought I should say that this is easily ten times the argument for why Muslim-in-life vampires would join the Lancea than anything I've seen from anyone else. (Most one-covenant arguments ultimately come down to ignoring history and religious forms as mere window-dressing, when to the covenants themselves they'd be critical - an argument <i>based</i> on those things is superior all round).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I assume that there are vampires who carry on their mortal religion (whether Islam or Christianity or Judaism or other), but these usually act alone and have not formed proper Covenants that can rival with the LeS. It is quite common for new vampires, too, to hang onto one's mortal religion for a while, but this is usually temporary. </div> </div> </div>I tend to think that groups formed around perpetuating a mortal religion would be more comparable to the Carthians than anything else, if only because Carthian is to some extent a catch-all for any minority political system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T00:16:27-07:00","id":1147336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Balancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/870083-lancea-et-sanctum?p=1144674#post1144674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A very serious Question regarding this Covenant.<br /> <br /> In the Second Edition is the &amp;quot;Book of Longinus &amp;quot; as it is printed in the first edition canon? There is a reference to the book of Longinus on page 42 but is it referenced as a generic text that the St can make whatever he wants or its the printed Book?<br /> <br /> I ask this that in the Second Editions and the printed material that followed the Covenants are purposely left vague except the basic tenets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, canon might be a bit too strong of a term. The Testament of Longinus is meant to be a physical prop to be used by STs and players in a very similar way the Book of Nod was used in VtM. The information is supposed to be in world accurate, although the book is written as a compilation done by several Kindred of the Sanctified and one of the Invictus. <br /> <br /> As for if it's still valid for 2nd Edition, well that's entirely up to the ST. That being said though...there is a Lancea et Sanctum specific story in Secrets of the Covenants that's entirely about a real Easter Egg that's in the Testament of Longinus. Take that as you will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T00:26:08-07:00","id":1147338,"title":"","content":"I'd just like to drop a reply off thanking Hermeticus for posting this. I've been rather unsatisfied with what I found superficial presentations of the Islamic and Judaic &quot;Creeds&quot; of the Lancea et Sanctum, but I haven't seen a perspective on the topic shared by a Muslim gamer until now, and you've provided me some further angles to chew on I hadn't considered.<br /> <br /> I do definitely incline your way in interpreting the Sanctified as something very different from vampires still dedicated to something resembling their faith from when they were alive. That contrast is fertile ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T03:51:00-07:00","id":1147357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/870083-lancea-et-sanctum?p=1147338#post1147338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd just like to drop a reply off thanking Hermeticus for posting this. I've been rather unsatisfied with what I found superficial presentations of the Islamic and Judaic &quot;Creeds&quot; of the Lancea et Sanctum, but I haven't seen a perspective on the topic shared by a Muslim gamer until now, and you've provided me some further angles to chew on I hadn't considered.<br /> <br /> I do definitely incline your way in interpreting the Sanctified as something very different from vampires still dedicated to something resembling their faith from when they were alive. That contrast is fertile ground.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're welcome! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T04:54:11-07:00","id":1147365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/870083-lancea-et-sanctum?p=1147357#post1147357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're welcome! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>As I mentioned earlier, your argument is based on the things that are going to matter to religiously oriented vampires, whereas most others have treated them as surface details not really important. An argument that can be made to and by the people in the setting is way more convincing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-07T12:24:21-07:00","id":1147850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/870083-lancea-et-sanctum?p=1147365#post1147365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I mentioned earlier, your argument is based on the things that are going to matter to religiously oriented vampires, whereas most others have treated them as surface details not really important. An argument that can be made to and by the people in the setting is way more convincing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do agree. The problem is that these arguments require training and disposition: training to know enough about the religious issues at stake (for example, I'm not just a Muslim, but one who has been lucky enough to receive both religious education and academic training in Islamic Studies and considerable exposition since youth to doctrinal differences between religions) and disposition to find doctrines, theology and philosophy important and interesting (to the point of making them important in one's setting in the game). It's normal and it's ok that most players, narrators and game-developers won't be like that and will emphasize other things in their characterization of covenants. Of course, a game developed with the assistance of a team of experts of real-world religions and ideologies who can help accurately flesh out each faction in the game would be awesome, but it would also cost a lot to produce...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}